\par\par \b \uc2  Poland Zloty Gains Midday, But  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Stands Aside \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 1997\par 13:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty has regained some ground midday Thursday after being down slightly against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  again confounded expectations by failing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second straight day, even as the zloty approached the level of 1% above the midpoint of the trading band. \par \par \uc2  Around 1045 GMT, the dollar was at 3.4010 zlotys, down from 3.4015 zlotys at the opening and from Wednesday's fixing of 3.4050 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.9418 zlotys, down from 1.9450 zlotys at the opening but up from Wednesday's fixing of 1.9360 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had given up trying to keep the zloty from rising to more than 0.5% above the midpoint of the band. They said 1% above the midpoint may constitute a new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. \par \par \uc2  'If we don't reach 1% today, then the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't enter the market,' said Malgorzata Sawicka, a trader at Bank Handlowy. 'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has decided to give us some freedom.' \par \par \uc2  But she and other dealers predicted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at some point as the zloty continues to move up against the basket, buoyed by foreign purchases of Polish securities. \par \par \uc2  Sawicka said news that former Finance Minister Leszek Balcerowicz may become deputy prime minister for economic affairs in the new government had given the zloty a boost. His appointment, she said, would further strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.4301 zlotys and for the mark at 1.9617 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 0.85% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 1.01% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.60% and 23.00%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-10-97 \par \par \uc2  1102GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dta907kxv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
