\par\par \b \uc2  Early zloty softens, seen gaining on foreign entry. \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Oct 6 (Reuter) - The zloty eased slightly against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket in early trade but dealers said that large foreign interest in Polish T-bills at Monday's auction could drive the local unit higher later today. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said that a zloty rise would probably set off a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Large cash-flows linked with foreign interset in T-bills and bonds are expected and the zloty should strengthen," said Katarzyna Plenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. "The zloty could rise to one percent if left unattended, but everything depends on where the NBP \b \highlight22\uc2 interveneves\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Plenny added. \par \par \uc2  At 0755 the zloty was at 0.47/0.42 percent from parity, against opening's 0.55/0.49 percent and Friday's 0.52/0.49. \par \par \uc2  It was at 3.4200/20 to the dollar, against opening's 3.4165/80 and at 1.9440/50 to the mark, against 1.9430/45. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was widely expected if the zloty firmed past resistance at 0.5-0.6 percent above the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors were seen entering Monday's 1.4 billion zloty T-bill tender in large number and driving down the average yield of the benchmark 52-week paper to below 23 percent from last week's 23.20 percent. \par \par \uc2  One-day rates held flat in slow morning trade after last week's NBP-bill sales and reverse repos drained excess cash from the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates were flat at 23.47/23.60 percent and tomorrow/next deposits flat at 23.45/23.60, both straddling the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main 14-day drainage rate of 23.55 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Wojciech Moskwa +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  E-mail: warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dta601j67\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
