\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Steady After Mkt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Earlier In Week \b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 1997\par 10:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty was steady against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket on Friday, with the market taking some respite after repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the week. \par \par \uc2  Around 0845 GMT, the dollar was at 3.4333 zlotys, little changed from 3.4323 zlotys at the opening and up from Thursday's fixing of 3.4220 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.9305 zlotys, up slightly from 1.9330 zlotys at the opening and down from Thursday's fixing of 1.9365 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  'There's pressure to sell hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for zlotys,' said Pawel Gajewski, assistant treasury manager at Creditanstalt. \par \par \uc2  Gajewski predicted the zloty would remain steady at 0.54% above the midpoint of trading band, but that it might break above that level in the early afternoon, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of the trading day would allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to set the fixing rate at around 0.5% above the midpoint, he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers predicted that continued heavy demand from foreign investors for Polish Treasury bills would pressure upward the zloty. The next auction is scheduled for Monday. \par \par \uc2  Some doubted whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be able to keep the zloty to within 0.5% of the midpoint in coming days. 'In the end they will capitulate and won't defend the level of 0.5%,' one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.4494 zlotys and for the mark at 1.9417 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 0.47% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 0.58% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 23.34% and 23.55%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-10-97 \par \par \uc2  0858GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dta307aj8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
