\par\par \b \uc2  Poland Zloty Steady Vs Basket Early As Foreign Demand Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 1997\par 11:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty is steady against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket early Thursday as it tracks dollar-Deutsche mark movement in international markets. \par \par \uc2  Around 0927 GMT, the dollar was at 3.4245 zlotys, down from 3.4278 zlotys at the opening but up from Wednesday's fixing of 3.4235 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.9343 zlotys, up from 1.9332 zlotys at the opening but down from Wednesday's fixing of 1.9350 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  'There is some buying of zlotys, but it's not very aggressive,' said Tomasz Wolosz, a dealer at Bank Rozwoju Eksportu. 'Demand is moderate.' \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they're wondering whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, as it has repeatedly since the beginning of the week. Wolosz said there would be no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the zloty continues to hold at less than 0.5% above the midpoint of the trading band. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars when the zloty rose to about 0.54% above the midpoint, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But Andrzej Fiderkiewicz, a dealer at Societe Generale, predicted that strong foreign demand for Treasury bills and bonds would push the zloty up beyond the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's informal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  barrier. \par \par \uc2  'The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  will definitely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' in the afternoon, he said, repeating the scenario of recent days. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.4468 zlotys and for the mark at 1.9417 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 0.65% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 0.38% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 23.00% and 23.45%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-10-97 \par \par \uc2  0948GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dta207bl0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
