\par\par \b \uc2  E. Europe Today -2: Poland President Meets ROP Leaders \b0\par\par\uc2 167 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 1997\par 08:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  In Poland, President Aleksander Kwasniewski continues a series of meetings with the leaders of political parties that won Parliamentary seats in the Sept. 21 election. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, Kwasniewski meets with leaders of the Movement to Rebuild Poland (ROP). Kwasniewski has asked Solidarity Electoral Action (AWS) to form a government. \par \par \uc2  Poland's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be watching to see if the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times since the Parliamentary election opened the gates for a rush of foreign investment in government securities. \par \par \uc2  In Romania, the Association Of Small And Medium-Sized Businesses will hold a national meeting in Bucharest Wednesday and press for changes to national tax law that members say are stifling small entrepreneurs. \par \par \uc2  The association says it will also release statistics outlining the situation of small and medium businesses in Romania. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 01-10-97 \par \par \uc2  0656GMT \par \par \uc2  1815 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dta107ap1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
