\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  Zloty/Amplifier -2: Correction Termed 'Cosmetic' \b0\par\par\uc2 274 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 1997\par 16:59\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the zloty rose more than 0.5% above the midpoint of its trading band against a basket of Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Even though the zloty is theoretically allowed to fluctuate within a 14-point band around the midpoint, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has now established an informal cap of 0.5% on the strong side of the midpoint, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  If not for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the zloty could move up more than 1% above the midpoint, said Piotr Czyzewski, a dealer at ING Bank. 'It has the strength,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was relatively mild and 'only slightly weakened the zloty,' said Wlodzimierz Osak, a dealer at Bank Polska Kasa Opieki SA. The result, he said, was a 'cosmetic correction' to the zloty's upward trend. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , participants said, is worried that a sudden influx of foreign capital seeking high yields on Polish government securities is pushing up the zloty at a time when the widening trade deficit is causing alarm. \par \par \uc2  If the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains too much, the reasoning goes, Poland's external balances could deteriorate further, eventually leading to a sudden withdrawal of foreign capital and a rapid depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The appetite of foreign investors for Polish securities was whetted by the Sept. 21 Parliamentary election, in which Solidarity Electoral Action (AWS) defeated the ruling Democratic Left Alliance (SLD). \par \par \uc2  On Monday, President Aleksander Kwasniewski asked AWS to form a coalition government. The coalition is widely expected to include the centrist Freedom Union (UW) party and perhaps others. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-09-97 \par \par \uc2  1459GMT \par \par \uc2  1195 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9t07f5r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
