\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty gains again capped by NBP  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Sept 23 (Reuter) - The zloty firmed on Tuesday as foreign investors were gradually warming up to Polish papers, but further strengthening may not come easy as the local unit's upside is closely guarded by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that foreign investor entry into treasuries lifted the zloty on Tuesday to about 0.6 percent above parity before a $25-$35 million \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back down to around 0.3 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign entry into bills and bonds gave the zloty an upward push today until the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved the market back down," said Marcin Trzykowski, dealer at Pekao SA. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed firmer at 0.40/0.29 percent above the trading band centre against Monday's 0.19/0.14 percent. It closed at 3.4420/35 to the dollar against 3.4445/55 on Monday and at 1.9180/95 to the mark against 1.9212/28. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the zloty was roughly between 0.45 percent and 0.30 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreigners would refrain from large scale entry until Poland's next cabinet crystalised after last Sunday's elections. A senior Solidarity source said on Tuesday his rightist bloc would rule with the market-trusted Union for Freedom (UW) liberals. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that if a strong Solidarity-UW coalition formed quickly the zloty may get a boost as such a government was seen ensuring much needed fiscal restraint in 1998. \par \par \uc2  One-day rates surged nearly three points as some large banks had gaps on their requried reserves and drained all surplus funds from the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates ended up at 25.50/26.50 percent against yesterday's 23.30/23.60 percent close. Tomorrow/next rates traded at 25.50/26.50 percent against 23.25/23.65. \par \par \uc2  Some said that one-day rates would hover around the 27-percent lombard rate on Wednesday, while others said rates would drop back down to around 24 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  E-mail: warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9n025sf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
