\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Down Against Basket In Volatile Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 1997\par 11:38\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty weakened against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket in volatile trading Tuesday, but started to gain ground again. \par \par \uc2  Around 0905 GMT, the dollar was at 3.4448 zlotys, up from 3.4415 zlotys at the opening and from Monday's fixing of 3.4445 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.9207 zlotys, down from 1.9210 zlotys at the opening and from Monday's fixing of 1.9210 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers reported considerable trading volume and said the market was unusually jumpy and volatile. \par \par \uc2  'It's total madness,' one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  One major order for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Polish unit of an international bank quickly lowered the zloty in early dealing, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  then started to recover, another dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The move was so large that some dealers suspected renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bought dollars for zlotys on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers predicted the zloty may start to move up again and test the level of 0.3% above parity at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  'There will be selling of dollars,' said Andrzej Fiderkiewicz, a dealer at Societe Generale. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.4493 zlotys and for the mark at 1.9283 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 0.13% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 0.39% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 21.70% and 22.00%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-09-97 \par \par \uc2  0938GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9n076nc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
