\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty eyes gains despite NBP  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  threat. \b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Sept 22 (Reuter) - The zloty is seen testing higher ground in the near-term on foreign inflows into Polish T-bills at Monday's auction despite the threat of another National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The foreign interest in T-bill auction may add to the zloty appreciation trend in the near-term," said Piotr Czyzewski, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at ING Bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that although a clear ceiling for the zloty was not created by the NBP, Monday's move signalled that the bank would closely monitor future zloty gains. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not operating with a set resistance level for the zloty, but it is watching for large intraday swings and it will closely eye zloty gains," said Malgorzata Sawicka, senior dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 0.19/0.14 percent above parity against Friday's 0.37/0.30 percent close after a $15 million \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It closed at 3.4445/55 to the dollar against 3.4260/80 on Friday and at 1.9212/28 to the mark against 1.9255/70. \par \par \uc2  At today's 1.44 billion zloty T-bill tender foreigners bought around 300 million zlotys of mainly 52-week bills. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign investors were mildly positive on Sunday's parliamentary election result, which left the rightist Solidarity alliance on the brink of power, most likely in a coalition with the liberals, who finished third in the vote. \par \par \uc2  One-day rates rose slightly on monthly tax payments, but were seen slipping lower on Tuesday as surplus liquidity was bound to return to the market. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates closed up at 23.10/23.50 percent against Friday's 22.80/23.30. Tomorrow/next rates traded at 23.25/23.65 percent against 22.20/23.00 percent. \par \par \uc2  -- Tomasz Oljasz +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  E-mail: warsaw.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9m023xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
