\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Opens Weaker After  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Monday \b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1997\par 11:37\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--Following \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the rise of the zloty Monday, the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened decidedly weaker Tuesday before regaining some ground. \par \par \uc2  By 0900 GMT the dollar was at 3.4875 zlotys, down from 3.5050 zlotys at the opening, and from Monday's fixing of 3.4730 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.8770 zlotys, unchanged from the opening, but up from Monday's fixing of 1.8710 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Monday after comments in the weekend press from a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official on the possibility of further rate increases to curb credit growth. The comments had set the Polish zloty racing as Polish banks speculated on a higher zloty. \par \par \uc2  Additional support was lent to the zloty by international investors' buying zlotys to invest in a bullish Warsaw Stock Market. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 12-08-97 \par \par \uc2  0937GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt8c05wdh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
