\par\par \b \uc2  Polish  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  caps bullish zloty at parity. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wojciech Moskwa \par \uc2 568 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 1997\par 16:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Aug 11 (Reuter) - The zloty jumped to its highest level in a month on Monday and had to be capped by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled it may tighten \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary screws. \par \par \uc2  In a Saturday newspaper a senior NBP official said the bank may again tighten monetary policy because commercial banks were not sufficiently raising credit and deposit rates after last week's official interest rate increase. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that foreign investors remained on the sidelines on Monday and that the zloty soared against the basket as domestic banks reduced foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions. \par \par \uc2  "There were no foreigners and domestic speculation and position adjustments gave the zloty a boost," said Wojciech Kowalczyk, senior dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  Some said large foreign capital inflows into the Warsaw bourse, which rose 5.2 percent on Friday and 3.3 percent on Monday, may have also boosted the zloty. \par \par \uc2  The zloty briefly climbed above the parity rate, the first time the local unit crossed the mid-point of its trading band since its mid-July decline amid mounting worries over flood losses, a gaping external deficit and parliamentary elections. \par \par \uc2  It closed at minus 0.26/0.31 percent from the trading band centre, against Friday's close at minus 0.73/0.88 percent after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought at least $20 million when the zloty was hovering slightly above the parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The zloty was at 3.4685/00 to the dollar, against 3.4850/00 on Friday and at 1.8690/00 to the mark, against 1.8750/80. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said, however, that despite recent gains the zloty would probably remain locked in a range between parity and minus 1.5 percent ahead of parliamentary polls on September 21. \par \par \uc2  "The NBP may have stabilised the market by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  because now the zloty resistance is at parity and the bank earlier gave the local unit support around minus 1.5 percent," said Witold Wozniak, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Deutsche Bank Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market's pro-zloty sentiment would likely run out of steam because longer-term foreign investors would likely stay clear of Polish treasuries ahead of elections and only speculators would dabble in the zloty in the coming month. \par \par \uc2  "This strengthening could be a short-term shot in the arm but the (up) trend could still be reversed ahead of elections," said Miroslaw Winiarczyk, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at BDK SA. \par \par \uc2  The NBP said in the Saturday paper its further monetary policy tightening would also depend on how the state-owned PKO BP - the country's biggest savings bank -- would react to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rate rise. \par \par \uc2  "We are still waiting for the reaction of (the state savings bank) PKO BP, but basically we already know that the hitherto (rate) increases in commercial banks are too small," NBP monetary policy head Jerzy Stopyra was quoted as saying. \par \par \uc2  "We may use other (monetary policy) instruments," he said. \par \par \uc2  On August 4 the NBP increased its lombard rate by two points to 27 percent and discount by 2.5 to 24.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The management board of PKO BP is due to meet on Tuesday to decide the bank's new rate levels after PKO sigalled that it would increase rates last week. \par \par \uc2  -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8b01czv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
