\par\par \b \uc2  Early zloty steadies around c.bank support. \b0\par\par\uc2 335 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, July 21 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty stabilised around expected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support levels at 3.5 percent below the parity rate early on Monday with no foreign orders to stir up trade so far, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that any prolonged zloty weakening past 3.5 percent below parity would probably be met with National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the NBP sold some $50 million on Friday to stop the zloty's decline. \par \par \uc2  "The market is waiting for NBP action if the zloty weakens but bids have so far remained around support," one \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer from a large Polish bank said. \par \par \uc2  At 0850 GMT the zloty was at -3.48/-3.63 percent from parity against -3.49/-3.89 percent at 0715 GMT. \par \par \uc2  It was at 3.4855/05 to the dollar, against 3.4850/950 at opening and at 1.9445/75 to the mark, against 1.9450/550. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said any zloty gains on the back of NBP action would be limited by foreign investor sales of Polish treasuries taking advantage of more favourable exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the NBP to raise official interest rates soon to cool credit action and offset additional government borrowing needed to finance relief of a weeks-long flood, which swamped more than one percent of Poland underwater. \par \par \uc2  On the money market one-day rates held flat as Monday's large 710 million zloty inflow created some short-term liquidity on the market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0900 GMT overnight rates were at 23.38/23.85 percent against opening's 23.60/23.75. Tomorrow/next were at 23.48/23.90 percent against 23.80/24.00 at 0655 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said interest rate rise expectations pushed up two- and three-month deposits to around the 25 percent lombard rate. \par \par \uc2  At 0905 GMT three month depos were quoted at 23.85/25.00 percent. -- Wojciech Moskwa +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7l0268c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
