\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Rises Vs Dlr After Reports Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 177 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1997\par 14:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty jumped against the dollar on Wednesday following unconfirmed reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 1230 GMT, the dollar was at 3.4425 zlotys, down from a peak of 3.5079 earlier in the day and from Tuesday's fixing of 3.5550 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  'The reaction was very strong' to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move to buy dollars for zlotys, said a dealer at ING Bank. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reportedly bought dollars at the level of 3.5220 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed that it wouldn't allow the zloty to slump to more than 5% below the parity rate. 'It gave the market direction,' the dealer at ING Bank said. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 16-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1246GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7g057fc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
