\par\par \b \uc2  Poland Zloty Decline Prompts Talk Of Devaluation \b0\par\par\uc2  By Christopher Wellisz \par \uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 1997\par 18:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The further rapid decline of the zloty on Tuesday - and the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - has prompted speculation that a one-off devaluation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be in the offing. \par \par \uc2  As the zloty lost about 1.7% of its value against the dollar Monday and a further 4.8% Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers awaited a move by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . None came. \par \par \uc2  In a highly regulated market such as \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's - where relatively small-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can have a huge impact - the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has come to be seen as a tacit acceptance of a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty trades in a 14-percentage point band around the central parity rate. On Tuesday, the zloty was nearing the limit of the weak side of the band against the dollar, sinking to 5.7% below the morning parity rate. \par \par \uc2  With the zloty nearing the edge of the band, analysts and traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy zlotys as early as Wednesday morning - or adjust the parity rate in such a way as to allow the zloty to move down within the existing exchange-rate mechanism. \par \par \uc2  'There is no way of halting the trend,' said Andrzej Fiderkiewicz, a dealer at Societe Generale in Warsaw. 'The zloty is overvalued right now.' \par \par \uc2  In trading Tuesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the dollar at 3.5550 zlotys, up from 3.3830 zlotys and the Deutsche mark at 1.9780 zlotys, up from 1.8885 zlotys Monday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 15-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1616GMT \par \par \uc2  1196 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7f05a86\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
