\par\par \b \uc2  Unknown Handlowy IPO inflows seen boosting zloty. \b0\par\par\uc2 355 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, June 17 (Reuter) - The zloty was bullish again on Tuesday as potential capital inflows into Bank Handlowy SA's one billion zloty IPO created strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling pressure. \par \par \uc2  But most of the market remains in the dark about the extent and timing of foriegn entry into Handlowy shares. \par \par \uc2  "There is a large amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market but it is not clear where it's coming from. Eveyone is looking at the Handlowy IPO but nobody is certain," said one dealer in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said Germany's Commerzbank AG further entry into Bank Rozwoju Eksportu SA (BRE) shares, cleared by the securites commision last week, also created upward pressure on the zloty. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 1.52/1.50 percent from the trading band centre, flat from Monday's close at 1.53/1.49 percent after the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) bought some $30-$50 million through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 3.2440/46 to the dollar, down from 3.2390/00 on Monday and at 1.8693/98 to the mark, up from 1.8703/13. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at 3.2450 zlotys, or when the zloty was about 1.52 percent from parity. \par \par \uc2  "The NBP will have problems in keeping the zloty at 1.5 percent from parity without \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  everyday," said Witold Wozniak, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Deutsche Bank Poska SA. \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry announced earlier on Tuesday that Poland will issue its first U.S. SEC-registered bonds in coming weeks, with JP Morgan leading the issue along with co-managers Merrill Lynch & Co. and Salomon Brothers Inc.. \par \par \uc2  The ministry did not give the amount of the issue, but under budget law Poland cannot issue more than $500 million worth of bonds on international markets in 1997. \par \par \uc2  The government will lower its official inflation target to year-on-year 12 percent in December this year from the current 13 percent plan, after price growth was smaller then expected in the first five months of 1997, the finance minister said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6h03xgy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
