\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty recaptures key resistance, awaits NBP action. \b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, June 17 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty again pushed above the key 1.5 percent from parity level in early Tuesday trade and the market waited for a National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the zloty back down below resistance. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty, propelled upward by foreign buying of Polish treasuries as well as other inflows, would probably remain bullish as the market had a surplus of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "(\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) selling continues today...and players expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act to reestablish resistance later in the session," said Tomasz Wolosz, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at BRE SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimated that on Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $45 million to keep the zloty from firming past 1.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  At 0850 GMT the zloty was quoted at 1.55/1.53 percent from the parity rate, up from opening's 1.49/1.45 percent from parity and Monday's close at 1.53/1.49 percent. \par \par \uc2  It was at 3.2430/40 to the dollar, down from opening's 3.2415/30 and at 1.8689/91 to the mark, up from 1.8725/35, in line with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise against the German unit. \par \par \uc2  Some expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying until late in Tuesday's session to lower its costs as trading volume often falls in the afternoon. \par \par \uc2  On the money market one-day rates inched up at offer after the NBP announced a 600 million zloty reverse repo and a 150 million NBP-bill sale, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0905 GMT overnight rates were at 21.55/22.00 percent, up from 21.60/21.80 percent at opening and tomorrow/next rates were at 21.70/22.00 percent, against Monday's 21.85/22.05. \par \par \uc2  The treasury said on Monday that it will offer 600 million zlotys of 52-week T-bills at an additional primary auction on Wednesday. The value date for this tender is Friday, June 20. \par \par \uc2  -- Wojciech Moskwa +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6h03xdt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
