\par\par \b \uc2  Polish zloty edges higher, waits for NBP action. \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, June 4 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty slowly inched up against the basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early Wednesday trade and players expected the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later today. \par \par \uc2  "If the zloty strenghtens past 1.5 percent from parity the NBP will most likely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...and the zloty is probably headed for higher levels today," said Malgorzata Sawicka, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market's recent pro-zloty sentiment as well as foreign entry prospects at today's fixed bond auction would give the zloty a boost on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  At 0855 GMT the zloty was at 1.54/1.51 percent from parity, above the 1.5 percent resistance level and stronger than 1.56/1.46 percent at 0705 GMT. \par \par \uc2  It was at 3.2270/80 to the dollar against opening's 3.2260/90 and at 1.8628/33 to the mark against 1.8625/45. \par \par \uc2  Late on Tuesday, Standard & Poor's affirmed Poland's BBB- long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating and its A- long-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating, while reviving the outlook to positive from stable on both ratings. \par \par \uc2  It also affirmed the A-1 short-term local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating and assigned the A-3 short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating. \par \par \uc2  "The ratings could be better but these results fall within market expectations. It does not bode ill for the zloty because S & P's outlook has improved," said Witold Wozniak, dealer at Deutsche Bank Polska SA. "Upward pressure on the zloty may even increase slightly on the rating update," he added. \par \par \uc2  One-day rates stabilised around 22.5 percent on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from staging any drainages. \par \par \uc2  At 0910 GMT overnight rates were at 22.30/22.50 percent, donw from 22.40/22.65 at opening and tomorrow/next were at 22.40/22.50 percent against Tuesday's close at 22.30/22.60. \par \par \uc2  -- Wojciech Moskwa +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6404k3o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
