\par\par \b \uc2  Polish zloty drifts at resistance, depos ease. \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juni 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, June 3 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty lingered a fraction below resistance at expected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels in slow early Tuesday trade without strong impetus to shade higher or lower, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said a light \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -selling trend remained on the market, which may later on Tuesday push the zloty into battle against National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if the local unit wondered far above 1.5 percent from parity. \par \par \uc2  "The 1.5 percent level should be guarded by the NBP and the zloty should trade between 1.45 to 1.55 percent, with a slight tendency for zloty gains," said Marcin Trzykowski of Pekao SA. \par \par \uc2  At 0852 the zloty was at 1.52/1.40 percent from parity, against opening's 1.55/1.45 percent and stronger than Monday's close at 1.49/1.38 percent. \par \par \uc2  It was at 3.2210/20 to the dollar, against opening's 3.2210/40 and at 1.8645/50 to the mark, against 1.8635/55. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market waited for foreign investor orders to set the tone of the market on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "The market seems set to return to speculating on dollar/mark moves unless some larger foreign orders materialise," Pekao's Trzykowski said. \par \par \uc2  On the money market overnight rates eased to 22.25 percent at bid from opening's 22.30/22.45 as the market continued to remain liquid despite larger outflows stemming from higher obligatory reserve, which were increased at the start of May. \par \par \uc2  "Banks created reserves for the larger outflows and short-term rates are not likely to be affected unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily drains the market," said Marek Wieczorkiewicz, chief dealer at PKO BP. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow/next rates were at 22.25/22.45 percent, slighly lower at offer from 22.25/22.55. \par \par \uc2  From the start of May, obligatory reserves on zloty call deposits increased by two points to 11 percent and by one point to five percent for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits. \par \par \uc2  The actual cash outflow from the increased reserves has occured from the start of June, as banks pay obligatory reserves according to the previous month's levels. \par \par \uc2  -- Wojciech Moskwa +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt6304ifi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
