\par\par \b \uc2  Poland  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -2: Price Reaction Muted \b0\par\par\uc2 159 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 1997\par 14:33\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets Wednesday at about 11:45 GMT, buying U.S. dollars for 3.1555 zlotys and Deutsche marks for 1.8490 zlotys, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have little immediate effect, with the market quoting the dollar at about noon GMT just a touch higher, at 3.1565 zlotys, and the mark at 1.8486 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  With the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  setting parity rates Wednesday of 3.2308 zlotys for the dollar and 1.8988 zlotys for the mark, the dollar was therefore trading at 2.30% below parity and the mark at 2.64% below at noon GMT. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks have been aimed at keeping the dollar-zloty and mark-zloty rates within 2.5% of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily parity rates. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-05-97 \par \par \uc2  1233GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt5e03gnq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
