\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty in no mood to tease c.bank, seen drifting. \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 25 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty made no attempt to rise above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -established resistance at 2.5 percent from the trading band centre and was seen drifting sideways for the rest of the day, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said that after five days of the zloty's uphill battle against the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  the Polish unit was likely to wait until Monday's primary T-bill tender before trying its luck again. \par \par \uc2  "The market is quiet and in the absence of foreign investors I do not expect any major moves today," said Mateusz Bieniek, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Societe Generale in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  At 0825 GMT the zloty was at 2.48/2.44 percent from the trading band centre against 2.52/2.46 percent at opening. It was at 3.1475/88 against the dollar, flat from 3.1465/90 at the opening and at 1.8349/54 against the mark from 1.8338/56. \par \par \uc2  On the money market overnight rates dropped to 5.0/15.0 percent from 9.0/12.0 percent at opening while tomorrow/next were at 14.0/20.0 percent from 19.2/20.2 percent on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "Rates fell because banks have surplusses on reserve accounts and they want to place cash for the weekend, with the end of the April reserve next week," said Adam Wrobel, money market dealer at Bank Hnaldowy SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drain the market with a combined reverse repo and NBP-bill sale \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  which could slightly lift T/N rates to 15.0/18.0 percent but said O/N rates were unlikely to be affected. \par \par \uc2  -- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4p06ml2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
