\par\par \b \uc2  Polish zloty,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to lock horns next week. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jan Strupczewski \par \uc2 531 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 25 (Reuter) - The zloty is poised to fight a lost battle against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday as foreign entry into T-bills and banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position cutting are likely to again pit it against \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign investors, eager to lock into high Polish T-bill yields amid falling inflation, would boost demand at Monday's 1.3 billion zloty tender and depress yields. \par \par \uc2  But dealers were mixed on the size of foreign entry. \par \par \uc2  "I would expect foreign demand to be at similar levels as last Monday, when it amounted to 1.7 billion zlotys, and just as last week, they might buy most of what is on offer," said Bartlomiej Kumela of Societe Generale in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  But others said that although foreigners were likely to come to the Monday tender, their interest was now more likely to turn to the 800 million zloty fixed bond auction on May 7. \par \par \uc2  "I would expect foreign bids at $100-150 million on Monday as the coming fixed bond tender will offer yet more attractive instruments," said Wojciech Kowalczyk of Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the 52-week yield on Monday to ease to 21.50-60 percent from 21.68 percent at the last tender. \par \par \uc2  They saw the 26-week and 13-week yield down to 21.50 percent from 21.69 and 21.74 percent respectively with the 8-week paper down to 21.30 percent from 21.46 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign bids at the T-bill tender would propel the zloty upward, above levels at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is certain step in with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland (NBP) said on Wednesday it wanted the zloty no higher than at 2.5 percent from the daily trading band centre after it pounded it for five days in a row with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  whenever it peeked above that level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that although only part of the foreign bids would come from new \b \highlight22\uc2 forex operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  as many investors were long on zlotys from deals done earlier this week and last week, the upward pressure on Polish unit would be strong. \par \par \uc2  "On Monday there will be the T-bill tender with foreign entry, but also banks will be cutting their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions to keep higher yielding zlotys over the long weekend," said Karol Zaluski of ING Bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Next Thursday and Friday are market holidays in \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "These two factors combined are likely to trigger an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the zloty's rise," Zaluski said. \par \par \uc2  On Friday the zloty around 2.47 percent from the parity rate, nearly flat from last week's close at 2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers also expected large liquidity swings on the money market on Monday and Tuesday -- the last two days of the April required reserve period. \par \par \uc2  Spreads on one-day rates widened to 5.0/21.0 percent on Friday amid excess liquidity, not alleviated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 343 million zloty reverse repo and a 750 million zloty NBP-bill sale. \par \par \uc2  -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4p06m1s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\s