\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty drifts sideways, may rise later, depos ease. \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 24 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty drifted just below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  firing line at 2.5 percent from parity in early trade, but dealers said it could tiptoe above it later today only to be punched down by a small-scale \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it was satisfied with the zloty's exchange rate no stronger than at 2.5 percent from the trading band centre after five days of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the bullish zoty down. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty might even weaken slightly in early trade and then inch up to or past the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  line at 2.5 percent and trigger NBP action," said Karol Zaluski of ING bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0830 GMT the zloty was at 2.48/2.45 percent from the parity rate, against 2.51/2.41 percent at opening. It was at 3.1490/00 against the dollar, down from 3.1460/95 at opening and 1.8320/25 against the mark, up from 1.8325/45. \par \par \uc2  "There might be some early zloty selling by banks' rebuilding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions cut on Wednesday, but there is a constant trickle of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  onto the market from foreigners and exporters," said Tomasz Nowakowski of Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty's move above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set resistance is not likely to be a bold one and the ensuing possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against it is likely to be cosmetic," he said. \par \par \uc2  Despite a net outflow of 406 million zlotys from the system on Thursday overnight rates on the money market traded at 19.70/19.90 percent, down from the opening 19.80/20.40 percent. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow/next cash was also lower at 19.50/21.00 percent against 19.90/20.80 percent at opening but dealers expected both rates to rise later today on the back of NBP drainages. \par \par \uc2  The NBP offered to drain 1.4 billion zlotys through a 14-day reverse repo rate with a T/N value date and 300 million through a sale of 91-day NBP-bills with O/N value date. The reverse repo rate was last at 22.15 percent and the 91-day bill average yield was 22.19 percent.-Jan Strupczewski +4822653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4o06k83\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
