\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty -2: NBP Tightening The Bank On Zloty \b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 1997\par 12:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Piotr Czyzewski, a trader at ING Bank in Warsaw, believed sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Thursday through Friday by the NBP was intended to show all that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not intend to allow bids on the dollar/zloty and mark/zloty to fall more than 2.5% below the parity rates the bank sets each day for the two rates. \par \par \uc2  Up until Thursday, a strong zloty had been trading against the dollar well in excess of 3% below the daily dollar/zloty parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The question now would be whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be able to sustain such a policy. \par \par \uc2  'Everything depends on foreign investors,' Czyzewski said, noting that it was aggressive buying of zlotys by foreigners early Thursday that had precipitated the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the NBP. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.2221 zlotys Friday and for the mark at 1.8732 zlotys. At 0945 GMT, the dollar was therefore trading at 2.55% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 2.39% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 21.60% and 21.80%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 18-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1029GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument 