\par\par \b \uc2  Polish NBP weakens zloty to help exports - analysts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jan Strupczewski \par \uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 18 (Reuter) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) this week has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the zloty while allowing real interest rates to rise to stimulate faster export growth while keeping a lid on imports, analysts said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday and Friday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought some $290 million and pounded the bullish zloty down to 2.5 percent from the trading band centre from above 3.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  It also kept its 273-day paper's average yield flat at 22.00 percent and its benchmark 14-day reverse repo rate at 22.15 percent on Friday despite a drop in inflation to 16.6 percent in March year-on-year from 17.3 percent in February. \par \par \uc2  The NBP, the finance ministry and independent economists agree Poland has every chance to bring inflation down to the targeted 13-percent year-on-year in December. \par \par \uc2  "The NBP is looking at \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trade balance, which is deteriorating, and is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the zloty to stimulate exports growth," said Andrzej Ladko, chief dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  "It also keeps high real interest rates to keep domestic demand down and thus cap imports growth," he said. \par \par \uc2  The bank has frequently expressed concern over the widening current account gap and said it would keep real interest rates rising to cool down domestic demand seen in the fast growth of credit for the economy. \par \par \uc2  Poland's current account deficit in February rose to $1.13 billion from $899 million in January against $1.35 billion in the whole of 1996. \par \par \uc2  The trade gap jumped to $2.18 billion in the first two months of this year from $706 million in January and $8.15 in the whole of 1996 as imports keep rising at about 30 percent in year-on-year terms and exports at about nine percent. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that to offset the monetary effect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered on Friday a huge 1.2 billion zloty reverse repo and a 300 million zloty sale of its 273-day bills -- the longest the bank has been selling. \par \par \uc2  "It is a safe moment because inflation is falling, but nevertheless the NBP sterilised the purchases with open market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday," said Zbigniew Chmielewski chief dealer at ING Bank in Wrasaw. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said for the weaker zloty to have an effect on Poland's foreign trade, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to keep the zloty anchored around the 2.5 percent from parity level for some time. \par \par \uc2  "If they did it to stimulate exports, they will have to keep that level for a while," said Marek Zelinski, analyst at Bank Slaski SA. \par \par \uc2  -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4i06s5t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
