\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Drops Vs Dollar On NBP  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1997\par 12:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty dropped sharply against the U.S. dollar in lively trading Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the zloty's appreciation. The NBP was seen buying both dollars at various levels, and Deutsche marks, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar opened at a level of 3.1225 zlotys, up from a fixing rate Wednesday of 3.1195 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The NBP then staged a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , first at a level of 3.1233 zlotys, most lately at a level of 3.1420 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  By around 1000 GMT, the dollar was significantly up, trading at a level of 3.1450 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark, meanwhile, was at 1.8215 zlotys at 1000 GMT, up from 1.8115 zlotys at the opening and from Wednesday's fixing rate of 1.8080 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.2267 zlotys Wednesday and for the mark at 1.8701 zlotys. At 1000 GMT, the dollar was therefore trading at 2.53% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 2.60% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 21.80% and 22.20%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1028GMT \par \