\par\par \b \uc2  Foreigners seek Polish bills as zloty forced down. \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 17 (Reuter) - Foreign investors, who bought small amounts of Polish treasuries over the last few weeks as yields reached a ceiling, were seeking T-bills on Thursday after a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled down the zloty. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreigners were searching for all types of paper but focused on 52-week T-bills after the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBP) dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled down the zloty by about half a percentage point in early Thursday trade. \par \par \uc2  "Foreign interest in Polish paper picked up as the exchange rate is much better at the moment," said Krzysztof Kozuchowski, T-bill dealer at ING bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  At 0910 GMT the zloty was at 2.87/2.72 percent from the parity rate, down from opening at 3.21/3.13 percent and Wednesday's close at 3.24/3.21 percent. \par \par \uc2  It was at 3.1355/00 to the dollar down from opening's 3.1220/50 and at 1.8155/85 to the mark, down from 1.8100/20. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last bought dollars at 0900 GMT at 3.1355 zlotys after first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday at 3.1233 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that foreign capital inflows into Polish paper would form a strong support for the zloty and could push the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back into \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  territory. \par \par \uc2  "Inflows into T-bills will put more upward pressure on the zloty and could set off further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action," said one dealer from a large Polish bank. \par \par \uc2  -- Wojciech Moskwa +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4h06yzc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
