\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2  Zloty Steady Vs Basket;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen Possible \b0\par\par\uc2 333 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1997\par 12:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty was steady against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket on Thursday despite a sudden dip in the dollar-Deutsche mark on international markets. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the zloty from moving up against the basket remained likely. They said the zloty would continue to strengthen in the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action. \par \par \uc2  Around 0953 GMT, the dollar was at 3.1130 zlotys, down from 3.1170 zlotys at the opening but up from Wednesday's fixing of 3.1095 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.8127 zlotys, up from 1.8110 zlotys at the opening and from Wednesday's fixing of 1.8100 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  'It was very hectic' at the start of trading, said Karol Zaluski of ING Bank. 'Dealers were afraid of taking positions because they didn't know what was going to happen with the dollar-mark.' \par \par \uc2  Zaluski said there appeared to be no definite short-term trend, but that the zloty was likely to continue gaining ground slightly in the longer term. \par \par \uc2  He said the zloty is getting a boost from remarks on Wednesday by Finance Minister Marek Belka that March inflation had likely fallen to an annual rate of 16.8%, down from 17.3% in February. 'The market took the news very favorably,' he said. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.2185 zlotys and for the mark at 1.8685 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 3.28% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 3.01% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.80% and 22.85%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 10-04-97 \par \par \uc2  1016GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4a02jt4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
