\par\par \b \uc2  Polish market braces for NBP zloty  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 10 (Reuter) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty during the next several trading sessions, with some dealers expecting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying as early as on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody knows when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it's just a question of time. In the past the NBP liked to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of a holiday or weekend, so it may very well step in tomorrow," said Pawel Gajewski, dealer at Creditanstalt SA. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday the zloty closed at 3.24/3.20 percent from the trading band centre, virtually unchanged from Wednesday's six-week high after a late charge recouped morning losses. \par \par \uc2  The zloty's afternoon rise was caused by banks cutting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions after dealers decided that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Earlier the zloty softened in nervous trade amid a volatile dollar/mark and expectations of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The zloty was at 3.1090/05 per dollar, down from 3.1080/00 on Wednesday and at 1.8118/25 to the mark, down from 1.8085/00. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign investors, the engine behind the zloty's recent charge, were not active in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade on Thursday and that nearly all of their $40 million worth of bids at today's 52-week T-bill auction were rejected. \par \par \uc2  At the auction the ministry kept the minimum price of the 52-week paper flat at Monday's level of 81.85, accepting 100 million zlotys of the 929 million worth of investor bids. \par \par \uc2  "The ministry signalled that it does not want to accept higher yields but it may have to because its cash flows are squeezed," said one dealer at a foreign bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the average 52-week bill average yield, listed at 21.93 percent, was actually in the region of 21.87 percent because the bills mature on a Saturday, April 11, 1998, and banks would have to wait for cash until the weekend ends. \par \par \uc2  One-day rates slipped below 23 percent on Thursday as a cash inflow and a large amount of rejected bids at the tender increased market liquidity, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates slipped to 22.40/24.85 percent from opening's 22.75/22.95 and tomorrow/next to 22.50/22.95 percent from 22.80/23.00. \par \par \uc2  -- Wojciech Moskwa +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4a075f1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
