\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Stable But Strong;  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Possible \b0\par\par\uc2 218 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1997\par 11:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty was stable against the U.S. dollar and Deutsche mark Wednesday, although its relative strength led traders to suggest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be a possibility if the zloty were to edge further up during the session. \par \par \uc2  Around 0930 GMT, the dollar was at 3.1125 zlotys, down slightly from 3.1135 zlotys at the opening, but up from Tuesday's fixing of 3.1075 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.8133 zlotys, up from 1.8120 zlotys at the opening and from Tuesday's fixing of 1.8120 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar Wednesday at 3.2090 zlotys and for the mark at 1.8710 zlotys. The dollar was therefore trading at 3.01% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 3.08% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 23.20% and 23.40%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 09-04-97 \par \par \uc2  0957GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt4902hp9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
