\par\par \b \uc2  Polish dealers split on NBP  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  prospects. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wojciech Moskwa \par \uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, April 8 (Reuter) - Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market dealers are divided on the prospects of National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, as such a move would spark more foreign interest in Polish treasuries. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the NBP has often \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local unit was more than three percent from the parity rate. On Tuesday the zloty finished around 3.15 percent from parity. \par \par \uc2  "It is not clear whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as such a move would make Polish T-bills even more attractive for foreigners. The odds are now 50-50," said Witold Wozniak, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Deutsche Bank Polska SA. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has often said that it planned to keep the zloty, traded within a 14 percent daily band around a central parity rate, volatile in the short-term to discourage speculative foreign capital flows. \par \par \uc2  Other dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday if the zloty tried to strengthen further amid foreign buying of Polish treasuries and investment inflows. \par \par \uc2  "If the zloty gains more ground tomorrow we may very well see an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Karol Zaluski of ING Bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty would be under additional upward pressure on Wednesday as banks shorten \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exposure to hold higher-yielding zloty positions over the week-end. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 3.17/3.13 percent from the trading band centre, stronger than Monday's close at 3.07/3.03 percent. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 3.1070/80 to the dollar, down from 3.0968/78 on Monday and at 1.8120/30 to the mark, up from 1.8191/01. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that on Tuesday the zloty remained locked under strong resistance at 3.1 percent from parity until about 1200 GMT, when players decided that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases for the rest of the day. \par \par \uc2  The zloty's charge on Tuesday was caused by foreign investor involvement in Monday's T-bill auction at which they bought an estimated $100 million as well as their entry into short-term bills in secondary trade on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "Foreigners were interested in buying two-month paper on Tuesday, but it's like walking on pins and needles because the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action," said Wojciech Kowalczyk, senior dealer at Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreigners would again bid for large amounts of Polish T-bills on Thursday, when the Treasury will hold an additional 500 million zloty tender of 52-week T-bills. \par \par \uc2  Some players said the months-long rise in Polish T-bill yields had likely ended and that the Treasury opted to hold the extra auction to show that yields had stopped their climb. \par \par \uc2  -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt4807isk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
