\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Opens Lower Vs Basket, Moves Up Slightly \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 1997\par 11:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty opened lower against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket but crept higher in nervous dealing on Thursday following the previous day's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0945 GMT, the dollar was at 3.0475 zlotys, down from 3.0535 zlotys at the opening and from Wednesday's fixing of 3.0555 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.8055 zlotys, up from 1.8030 zlotys at the opening but down slightly from Wednesday's fixing of 1.8060 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's decline against the zloty was partly a reflection of its weakness against the mark, dealers said. But in part it was a also caused by demand for zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was still upward pressure on the zloty. Nevertheless, said Pawel Gajewski of Creditanstalt, the zloty is at 'a level that should satisfy' the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  three times on Wednesday to buy dollars for zlotys. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at 3.0337 zlotys, 3.0355 zlotys and 3.0360 zlotys. Dealers estimated the scale of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at about $25 million. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.1450 zlotys and for the mark at 1.8576 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 3.20% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 2.88% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 20.50% and 20.80%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 20-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1002GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2k01766\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
