\par\par \b \uc2  Polish c.bank dollar buying send zloty tumbling. \b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Feb 19 (Reuter) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought an estimated $30 million through \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, pulling the rug out from under the zloty and re-establishing three percent from parity as resistance. \par \par \uc2  "Today's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  means the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants three percent from the parity rate to be the barrier," said Przemyslaw Ciszecki, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at ING Bank in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the NBP first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the zloty strengthened to 3.6 percent from the parity rate and knocked it down more than half a percentage point by close. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggested that 3.5 percent from parity is too strong and that three percent is where the zloty should be," said Magloszata Sawicka from Bank Handlowy SA. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 2.98/2.75 percent from the trading band centre, down from Tuesday's 3.58/3.50 percent close. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 3.0500/60 to the dollar, down from 3.0360/80 on Tueday and at 1.8035/80 to the mark, down from 1.7845/65. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at serveral levels today, with the latest round of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 3.0531 zlotys per dollar and 1.8040 zlotys per mark, which is about 2.91 percent from the trading band centre. \par \par \uc2  Several dealers said that before the NBP started buying \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday some foreign investors began to sell small amounts of Polish treasuries to take advantage of the relatively strong zloty exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the zloty may be under further upward pressure in the near-term as foreign investors were expected to bid for larger amounts of Polish 12-percent five-year fixed bonds at Thursday's 200 million zloty primary auction. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which knocked the zloty down, were a present for foreign investors who are hungry for Polish fixed bonds," said one dealer at a major London bank. \par \par \uc2  On the money market one-day rates eased as banks found excess cash after squaring reserve positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates fell to 20.75/21.20 percent from opening's 21.10/21.45 percent and tomorrow/next rates to 21.80/21.15 percent from Tuesday's close 21.25/21.65. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said that money market liquidity increased because banks started selling bonds from their portfolios in anticipation of yield increases at future auctions. \par \par \uc2  -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dt2j003se\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
