\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Opens Down Vs Dollar, But Gains Quickly \b0\par\par\uc2 228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 1997\par 11:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty opened lower against the dollar but then moved up quickly before stabilizing in active dealing on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Around 0959 GMT, the dollar was at 3.0385 zlotys, down from 3.0420 zlotys at the opening but up from Friday's fixing of 3.0310 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.7948 zlotys, down from Friday's fixing of 1.7985 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was considerable demand for the Polish \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from foreign investors and from Polish exporters. \par \par \uc2  With the zloty inching up against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket over the past several days, dealers said the probability of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared high. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.1390 zlotys and for the mark at 1.8536 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at about 3.31% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 3.28% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.90% and 23.25%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1004GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2h00zqv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoa