\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 's Zloty Steady Vs Basket; No  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Seen \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 1997\par 11:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty was steady against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket on Tuesday, with dealers saying \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely in the absence of a sudden upward move. \par \par \uc2  Around 1020 GMT, the dollar was at 3.0131 zlotys, up from 3.0100 zlotys at the opening and from Monday's fixing of 3.0025 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.8075 zlotys, down from 1.8105 zlotys at the opening and from Monday's fixing of 1.8150 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the zloty was tracking movements in the dollar-mark on international markets and that the market was calm after a brief flurry of dollar selling shortly after the opening. \par \par \uc2  Piotr Nurzinski, a dealer at Polski Bank Inwestycyjny, noted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had fixed the dollar and mark at an average of about 3% below their fixing rates on Monday afternoon. \par \par \uc2  'That shows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is willing to tolerate a 3% deviation' from the central parity rate, Nurzinski said. 'I don't expect \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the deviation goes well above 3%,' he said. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.1036 zlotys and for the mark at 1.8653 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 3.00% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 3.20% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.25% and 22.65%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 11-02-97 \par \par \uc2  1028GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt2b00xwj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
