\par\par \b \uc2  RECENT ZLOTY RISE NOT ON FOREIGN INFLOWS- C.BANK. \b0\par\par\uc2 289 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Jan 28 (Reuter) - The rise of the Polish zloty to four percent from the centre of the trading band, which triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was not fuelled by foreign inflows, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Witold Kozinski told a news conference that had fresh foreign funds been flowing into the system, banks repeatedly hit by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases would not need to buy \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  back from the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "On January 20 we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time...taking the zloty down to three percent from about 4.1 percent by buying $90 million, but at the post trade fixing banks come to the NBP to buy back as much as $60 million," Kozinski said. \par \par \uc2  "It was a clear signal that the strengthening of the zloty was not, in any way, connected to higher supply of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he added. \par \par \uc2  The NBP \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the zloty again on Wednesday and Friday and in all three instances, Kozinski said, banks sustained losses. \par \par \uc2  "The bottom line is that the zloty's rise was created... mostly by unidentified factors...to a small extent because of the dollar/mark cross...and in the least by a supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  Last week dealers said the zloty's bullish mood was fuelled mostly by foreign inevstors taking Polish positions at the start of the year, attracted by high real interest rates and expectations of a cut in the zloty's monthly devaluation rate. \par \par \uc2  They also noted Poland's plans to meet European Monetary Union's requirements for joining in 2004 and better than expected 1996 fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  -- Jan Strupczewski +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020040131dt1t00aof\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
