\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Poland \highlight\uc2 /Limits/Investment -4:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  On  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 1997\par 08:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Creamer estimated that foreigners have about $1 billion invested in Polish government debt, down from a peak of about $2 billion in 1995. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently fears that the zloty's strength may start to attract more foreign investors to government paper. That's because a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  increases dollar yields on zloty-denominated investments. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to drive the zloty lower against the dollar and the Deutsche mark. The dollar and mark have the heaviest weightings in the basket of five \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to which the zloty is pegged. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also was prompted by concerns about the growing trade and current-account deficits, National Bank of Poland Vice President Witold Kozinski told a press conference Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  'The trade balance cannot get worse,' Kozinski said. 'We must do something to stabilize it.' He called the zloty's strength 'groundless' given the growing trade gap. \par \par \uc2  In November, Poland's current-account deficit widened by $125 million to stand at $984 million for the first 11 months of 1996, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The trade deficit widened by $805 million in November to rise to $7.2 billion for the first 11 months of the year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been pushing interest rates higher in recent months by draining liquidity from the money market via open-market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Since the end of November, overnight deposit rates for zlotys have risen 2.5 percentage points to about 21%. \par \par \uc2  Falling inflation, rising interest rates and a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  create a 'perfect environment for fixed income' investments, said Krzysztof Bledowksi, an economist at WoodCommerz in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 29-01-97 \par \par \uc2  0746GMT \par \par \uc2  1141 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1t00itl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
