\par\par \b \uc2  Foreign-charged zloty rises, Polish c.bank looks on. \b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Jan 28 (Reuter) - The zloty returned to the offensive on Tuesday, rising against the basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid foreign investor entry in Polish bonds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said that the Polish market, still shell-shocked from repeated National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week, cautiously inched up during today's session waiting for an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which did not materialise. \par \par \uc2  "The zloty, likely charged by foreign entry into Polish treasuries, gradually strengthened on Tuesday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Piotr Czyzewski of ING Bank in Warsaw. "But they could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any moment now." \par \par \uc2  However, some said that money market rates could rise by as much as one percentage point as liquidity drops before the new higher deposit requirements take effect on February 28. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday overnight rates inched up to close at 21.25/21.45 percent versus opening's 21.05/21.17 percent as cash flows tightened for end-of-month reserve squaring. \par \par \uc2  Tomorrow/next rose to 21.40/21.65 percent from 21.10/21.25. \par \par \uc2  -- Wojciech Moskwa +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt1s02kco\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
