\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Gains Against Dollar and Deutsche Mark \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 1997\par 11:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty continued to gain against both the dollar and Deutsche mark Friday as foreign investors sold hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to invest in shares and Treasury bills, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'The market has gone mad,' said a dealer at Creditanstalt. 'There's sharp selling' of the dollar, he said. 'It's totally irrational.' \par \par \uc2  Around 1025 GMT, the dollar was at 2.9060 zlotys, down from 2.9115 zlotys at the opening but up from Thursday's fixing of 2.8701 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.8127 zlotys, down from 1.8165 zlotys at the opening and from Thursday's fixing of 1.8200 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  Early dollar selling was followed by a lull on the market. 'There's no buying (of dollars) at the moment,' said the Creditanstalt dealer. 'Everybody's afraid to buy. The only thing that can change the situation is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  However, this dealer and others said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared unlikely, at least for the time being. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at 3.0190 zlotys and for the mark at 1.8850 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 3.89% below its parity rate, and the mark was at 3.99% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 21.45% and 21.55%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-01-97 \par \par \uc2  1040GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt1h00cgk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
