\par\par \b \uc2  Poland's Zloty Continues To Strengthen Against Basket \b0\par\par\uc2 321 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1996\par 10:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  WARSAW (AP-Dow Jones)--The Polish zloty continued to strengthen against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket on Wednesday as dealers wondered whether and when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Around 0910 GMT, the dollar was at 2.8615 zlotys, down from 2.8633 zlotys at the opening and from Tuesday's fixing of 2.8625 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Deutsche mark was at 1.8370 zlotys, down from 1.8375 zlotys at the opening but up from Tuesday's fixing of 1.8300 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  '\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible,' said Bogdan Stepkowski of ING Bank. 'But it's hard to tell what their policy is, or what deviation from the parity rate they will tolerate.' \par \par \uc2  Amid the uncertainty, banks are dealing cautiously, said Tomasz Wlad of Amerbank. 'Lots of banks are testing the market,' he said, 'but not many are actually doing anything.' \par \par \uc2  Wlad added, however, that the pressure for the sale of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had abated somewhat from Monday. 'There's no visible trend,' he said. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers attributed the zloty's strength to lack of liquidity and high rates on the money market. Corporations are typically in need of cash in December, when they must pay taxes for two months at once, Stepkowski said. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of Poland set the parity rate for the dollar at 2.9402 zlotys and for the mark at 1.8887 zlotys. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty is fixed to a basket of five Western \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and is devalued at a rate of 1% per month. It is allowed to fluctuate within plus or minus 7% of the central parity rate. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 2.75% below its parity rate, while the mark was at 2.81% below its parity rate. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market rates were indicated at between 22.00% and 24.00%. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 04-12-96 \par \par \uc2  0936GMT \par \par \uc2  1167 1854 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011014dsc401juo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
