\par\par \b \uc2  Polish zloty firms again, depos up on dry market. \b0\par\par\uc2 433 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 1996\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1996 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Dec 4 (Reuter) - The Polish zloty strengthened to a new six month high at more than 2.7 percent from the trading band centre on Wednesday after a week-long \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -selling trend continued this morning, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -selling sentiment was not as strong as in past days, but large enough to set a new peak for the zloty, the highest from late May's three percent from parity. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that the sentiment faded by mid-morning and left the zloty drifting in line with dollar/mark swings. \par \par \uc2  "After some early \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling the zloty was left to track dollar/mark," said Marcin Turkiewicz of Bank Zachodni SA. \par \par \uc2  The zloty closed at 2.74/2.71 percent from the trading band centre, stronger than Tuesday's close at 2.67/2.63 percent. \par \par \uc2  It closed at 2.8632/40 to the dollar, down from 2.8625/33 on Tuesday and at 1.8341/47 marks, down from 1.8300/10. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the cental bank would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenue\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stop the zloty's gains, as it had done earlier this year, as long as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows resulted from privatisation or capital increases of foreign banks in Poland. \par \par \uc2  "As long as the inflow of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is structural and not speculative the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," one dealer at a Polish bank said. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Poland\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBP) last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on May 22 when the NBP bought dollars at about three percent from the average dollar and mark parity rates. \par \par \uc2  The money market remained tight with most players searching for cash, which kept one-day deposit bids at a high level of 23 percent and dealers said the shortage may continue in upcoming days as there were no large inflows later this week. \par \par \uc2  "Big banks sought funds even for longer periods. This might be the market's response to the NBP's recent statement that market rates may rise," said Elzbieta Adamska from BIG SA. \par \par \uc2  The NBP had signalled last month that market rates may rise in upcoming months to cap excessive growth of credit action. \par \par \uc2  Overnight rates were at 23.00/24.50 percent against the opening at 23.00/24.00 percent. Tomorrow/next rates were at 23.40/24.30 percent against 23.50/24.20 pct at 0950 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The NBP had not staged an open market opertation since November 28. \par \par \uc2  -- Krzysztof Wojcik +48 22 653 9700 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1996 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dsc402nhu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
